<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n31163" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴποτε</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ ποτε</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>if
			ever</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.39
			</span></i>; strengthd. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴ ποτε δή</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				503
			</span></i>: used in asking a favour of any one, to call something to
			his mind, for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἴποτ᾽ ἔην γε</span>,
			i.e. <i>as surely as</i> he was. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> indirect, <i>if</i> or <i>whether
			ever</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.97
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
